      "problem": "$\\frac{6{x}^{4}-6{x}^{3}+5{x}^{2}-x+7}{2{x}^{2}-2x+1}=$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,3{x}^{2}+1 \\\\  & 2{x}^{2}-2x+1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,6{x}^{4}-6{x}^{3}+5{x}^{2}-x+7\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{6{x}^{4}-6{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2{x}^{2}-x+7 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\,2{x}^{2}-2x+1}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,x+6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nAs a result,\n\n- the quotient is $3{x}^{2}+1,$ and\n\n- the remainder is $x+6.$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\frac{6{x}^{4}-6{x}^{3}+5{x}^{2}-x+7}{2{x}^{2}-2x+1}=3{x}^{2}+1+\\frac{x+6}{2{x}^{2}-2x+1}.\n$$",
